<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    RDR-191 Phase 5 (bead nexus-o8dil.49) — the UNIFIED collection-registry
    FK on nexus.chunks: the successor of fk-002's three per-dim collection
    FKs (chunks_384_collection_fk / chunks_768_collection_fk /
    chunks_1024_collection_fk), which died automatically as a side effect of
    vectors-004-unify-chunks.xml's DROP TABLE ... CASCADE (a constraint
    cannot outlive its table — see that changeset's own "fk-002 NOTE"
    header, and this bead's 2026-08-13 comment). The DROP-half of the
    original bead scope is therefore moot; this changelog ships only the
    ADD-half, on the unified table, for the collection axis (chunks(tenant_id,
    collection) -> catalog_collections(tenant_id, name)) — NOT to be
    confused with catalog-029's manifest FK (catalog_document_chunks ->
    nexus.chunks), a different table pair entirely.

    THREE-STEP SHAPE, mirroring fk-002's own ADD-NOT-VALID -> reconcile ->
    VALIDATE choreography (fk-002-collection-registry.xml / fk-002-validate.xml):

      1. fk-004-0: ADD CONSTRAINT ... NOT VALID.
      2. fk-004-1-reconcile: ADDITIVE parent-stub reconcile — INSERT ...
         ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING into catalog_collections from nexus.chunks'
         OWN distinct (tenant_id, collection) values. This is fk-002-6-
         reconcile's shape for THIS direction (chunks -> catalog_collections
         registry rows), never destructive — matching the o8dil.23 Phase-5
         planning pass's SHAPE NOTE: "for THIS FK the missing parent is a
         registry row, so fk-002-6-reconcile's additive stub-backfill
         precedent applies directly." Because the reconcile derives every
         stub row FROM nexus.chunks' own values, it is IMPOSSIBLE for this
         step to leave a row in nexus.chunks whose collection is not
         registered afterward — the "violating row" MUST-FAIL test below
         therefore exercises the FK's actual guard mechanism directly (bare
         VALIDATE without this reconcile step), not a data scenario this
         changelog's own forward path can produce.
      3. fk-004-2: new-id VALIDATE CONSTRAINT, guarded per the project's
         blanket "every bare VALIDATE CONSTRAINT is guarded" tripwire
         (tests/test_changelog_validate_precondition_lint.py) with a
         whole-changeset <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN"> naming the
         constraint — identical shape to catalog-029-2 and fk-002-7..11.

    All three are ORDINARY RUN-ONCE changesets (no runAlways). No LOCK TABLE
    is needed before the reconcile: fk-004-0 (this same file, always runs
    first in the same walk) already enforces every NEW write from the
    instant it commits, so by the time fk-004-1-reconcile runs, only
    PRE-EXISTING rows can possibly be unregistered — the identical
    reasoning catalog-029-1's header gives for skipping its own LOCK TABLE.

    RLS DISCIPLINE (fk-004-1-reconcile only; fk-004-0/2 are pure DDL/VALIDATE,
    no DML): nexus.chunks (vectors-004-unify-chunks.xml) and
    nexus.catalog_collections (catalog-001-baseline.xml changeset 7) both
    carry FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY. Liquibase runs as nexus_admin, the table
    owner but NOT BYPASSRLS — under FORCE RLS with no nexus.tenant GUC set
    at migration time, an untoggled read of nexus.chunks would see ZERO rows
    (the reconcile INSERT ... SELECT would silently register nothing), and
    an untoggled INSERT into catalog_collections would fail every row's
    WITH CHECK (tenant_id = current_setting('nexus.tenant', true), which is
    NULL at migration time). Both tables are toggled NO FORCE, then restored
    to FORCE, symmetrically, inside fk-004-1-reconcile's own changeset
    (catalog-029-1 toggle-wrapped shape).

    FK SHAPE: FOREIGN KEY (tenant_id, collection) REFERENCES
    catalog_collections (tenant_id, name) ON DELETE RESTRICT NOT VALID —
    the EXACT shape fk-002-1/2/3 used for chunks_384/768/1024 (no ON UPDATE
    CASCADE: a collection rename re-homes chunk rows explicitly via
    CatalogRepository#renameCollection's coherent INSERT-new/re-home/DELETE-
    old sequence, RDR-164 P3, never a bare UPDATE catalog_collections SET
    name — see fk-003's own "ON UPDATE SEMANTICS" header for the identical
    house rule applied to its five FKs). MATCH SIMPLE (the PostgreSQL
    default): nexus.chunks.collection is NOT NULL from creation
    (vectors-004-unify-chunks.xml step 1), so MATCH SIMPLE's null-exemption
    is structurally inert here, same disclosure as catalog-029's header.

    Must come after catalog-029-manifest-chunk-fk.xml (registered immediately
    after it in db.changelog-master.xml, matching every other late-appended
    changelog's file-order convention) and, transitively, after the RDR-191
    Phase 4 repoint batch (nexus.chunks, the FK's referencing table, does not
    exist before vectors-004-unify-chunks.xml runs).

    STALE-PROSE CORRECTIONS (this bead's acceptance criterion): the header
    comments at db.changelog-master.xml naming the fk-002/fk-002-validate
    <include> entries, and fk-002-collection-registry.xml / fk-002-validate.xml's
    own file headers, are updated in this SAME diff to record that the three
    per-dim chunks_<dim>_collection_fk constraints those files added are now
    DEAD (retired automatically by vectors-004's DROP TABLE ... CASCADE, not
    by any action in THIS file) rather than leaving the stale "P0.2/P0.3"
    framing as though those constraints were still live. Comment edits only,
    OUTSIDE the frozen <changeSet> bodies — fk-002-1..5/fk-002-6..11's own
    <sql>/<preConditions> content is untouched (checksum-frozen, already
    applied).

    fk-002-7..11 / fk-003-7..11 VACUITY DISPOSITION (this bead's acceptance
    criterion): fk-002-7/8/9's <preConditions> sqlCheck each count
    pg_constraint rows named 'chunks_<dim>_collection_fk' — constraints
    that no longer exist (dropped with their tables by vectors-004's
    CASCADE). Per nexus-4m6i0.13's MARK_RAN freeze semantics (documented in
    fk-002-validate.xml's own header and in
    tests/test_changelog_validate_precondition_lint.py), a missing-constraint
    precondition marks the changeset ran (once, harmlessly) rather than
    hard-failing — these three changesets therefore MARK_RAN-skip on every
    box from this release forward, permanently, and do NOT brick anything.
    fk-002-10/11 (chash_index_collection_fk, topic_assignments_collection_fk)
    remain live and unaffected — their tables/constraints still exist.
    fk-003-7..11 similarly remain fully live (fk-003's five child tables —
    document_aspects, aspect_extraction_queue, topics, taxonomy_meta,
    document_highlights — were never touched by vectors-004's CASCADE).
    No new-id VALIDATE supersedes fk-002-7/8/9: there is nothing left to
    validate (their target constraints are gone), and this file's own
    fk-004-2 VALIDATE is the successor for the SURVIVING invariant (the
    unified table's own collection FK), not a replacement for the retired
    per-dim ones. Disposition recorded here per this bead's acceptance
    criterion ("document ... rather than editing frozen bodies").
-->
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.4.xsd">

    <!-- ── Changeset fk-004-0: ADD CONSTRAINT ... NOT VALID ─────────────────── -->
    <changeSet id="fk-004-0" author="nexus-o8dil.49">
        <comment>
            chunks_collection_fk: FOREIGN KEY (tenant_id, collection) REFERENCES
            nexus.catalog_collections (tenant_id, name) ON DELETE RESTRICT NOT
            VALID -- the unified successor of fk-002-1/2/3 (chunks_384/768/1024
            -> catalog_collections), which died with their tables. NOT VALID:
            enforces every new write immediately; retroactive validation of
            pre-existing rows is fk-004-1-reconcile (additive stub-backfill)
            then fk-004-2 (VALIDATE).
        </comment>
        <sql splitStatements="true" stripComments="false">
ALTER TABLE nexus.chunks
    ADD CONSTRAINT chunks_collection_fk
    FOREIGN KEY (tenant_id, collection)
    REFERENCES nexus.catalog_collections (tenant_id, name)
    ON DELETE RESTRICT
    NOT VALID;
        </sql>
        <rollback>
            ALTER TABLE nexus.chunks DROP CONSTRAINT IF EXISTS chunks_collection_fk;
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

    <!-- ── Changeset fk-004-1-reconcile: additive parent-stub reconcile ─────── -->
    <changeSet id="fk-004-1-reconcile" author="nexus-o8dil.49">
        <comment>
            Additive stub-register: INSERT INTO catalog_collections SELECT
            DISTINCT (tenant_id, collection) FROM nexus.chunks ON CONFLICT DO
            NOTHING -- fk-002-6-reconcile's shape, applied to nexus.chunks'
            own values. Never destructive (no DELETE arm): a chunk row is real
            data (chunk_text + an embedding), so an "orphan" here gets its
            missing registry parent stub-created, exactly like fk-002's own
            per-dim precedent for the identical vector-serving-layer tables
            (fk-002-validate.xml's own header: "an orphan chunk is real data,
            not lifecycle debris -- deleting it would be data loss"). RLS
            toggle-wrapped (nexus-1wjmq shape): both nexus.chunks and
            nexus.catalog_collections carry FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY and
            Liquibase's nexus_admin owner is not BYPASSRLS, so both are
            toggled off for the INSERT...SELECT and restored before this
            changeset ends.
        </comment>
        <sql splitStatements="false" stripComments="false">
ALTER TABLE nexus.chunks NO FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE nexus.catalog_collections NO FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

INSERT INTO nexus.catalog_collections (tenant_id, name)
SELECT DISTINCT tenant_id, collection
FROM nexus.chunks
ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, name) DO NOTHING;

ALTER TABLE nexus.catalog_collections FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE nexus.chunks FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
        </sql>
        <rollback>
            <!-- No rollback: stub rows are inert; the FK being added is dropped
                 by fk-004-0's own rollback. Removing stubs here could break
                 existing references (fk-002-0's own precedent). -->
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

    <!-- ── Changeset fk-004-2: VALIDATE CONSTRAINT ──────────────────────────── -->
    <changeSet id="fk-004-2" author="nexus-o8dil.49">
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN">
            <sqlCheck expectedResult="1">SELECT COUNT(*) FROM pg_constraint WHERE conname = 'chunks_collection_fk'</sqlCheck>
        </preConditions>
        <comment>
            VALIDATE chunks_collection_fk -- retroactively check pre-existing
            rows now that fk-004-1-reconcile has stub-registered every
            collection nexus.chunks references. Guarded by a whole-changeset
            precondition (nexus-4m6i0.13/catalog-029-2 shape): skips (marks
            ran, once) instead of hard-ERRORing a crash-loop boot on any box
            where the constraint doesn't exist. All three fk-004 changesets
            ship together in one file/release, so fk-004-0 always runs first
            in the same walk and this guard is expected to be a permanent
            no-op in practice -- added purely to satisfy the project's
            blanket "every bare VALIDATE CONSTRAINT is guarded" tripwire
            (tests/test_changelog_validate_precondition_lint.py).
        </comment>
        <sql splitStatements="true" stripComments="false">
ALTER TABLE nexus.chunks VALIDATE CONSTRAINT chunks_collection_fk;
        </sql>
        <rollback>
            <!-- VALIDATE cannot be un-done (no INVALIDATE in PG); the constraint
                 itself is dropped by fk-004-0's rollback. -->
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
